==============================================================================
C.  SENSITIVITY -- boundary rule, stars, truncation, weights
==============================================================================

   C1  boundary rule.  Run Z showed the rule DEFINES the variable, so
       every defensible rule is run and the primary was declared first.
       fixed10Mpc                 beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]  (edge)
       fixed5Mpc                  beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]  (edge)
       fixed3Mpc                  beta = +1.250   68% [+1.250, +1.500]
       2xR500                     beta = +0.500   68% [+0.500, +0.750]
       10xrs                      beta = +2.000   68% [+1.750, +2.000]  (edge)

   C2  truncation radius of the dynamical density.  Under the RAR the
       outer dynamical density falls as r^-2, so Sigma depends on r_t
       logarithmically -- this is a real systematic, not a grid choice.
       r_t = 10 Mpc               beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]  (edge)
       r_t = 20 Mpc               beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]  (edge)
       r_t = 40 Mpc               beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]  (edge)

   C3  stellar baryons.  The eFEDS tables give no stellar mass, so M_b
       is gas only in the primary; these are uniform rescalings of M_b.
       f_star = 0.00            beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]
       f_star = 0.15            beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]
       f_star = 0.30            beta = +2.000   68% [+2.000, +2.000]

   C4  stacking weights
       inverse shape noise        beta = +2.000
       equal weights              beta = +1.000
       uncapped aperture          beta = +1.250

   C5  radial range (the paper excludes R < 0.5 h^-1 Mpc from its own
       fiducial fit because of miscentering)
       R > 0.5 h^-1 Mpc (fiducial) beta = +2.000  (7 bins)
       all ten bins               beta = +2.000  (10 bins)
       R > 1 h^-1 Mpc             beta = +2.000  (4 bins)

==============================================================================
F.  POWER -- what the PRIVATE per-cluster profiles would deliver
==============================================================================

   The 313 per-cluster shear profiles exist; they are simply not published.
   This is the Fisher forecast for the experiment they would allow, with the
   noise model already validated in B0 against the published stacked errors.
   The competitor is carried in the SAME Fisher matrix: if beta and a bare
   radius tilt gamma are degenerate even with per-cluster data, the experiment
   cannot decide the question no matter how much shear is available.

   328 systems, 10 radial bins each, shape noise sigma_e = 0.4, aperture cap 20'
   predicted total S/N of the per-cluster ensemble 14.6   (published stacked S/N 29.0)

   sigma(beta), nothing else free                0.0269
   sigma(beta), free amplitude (class step)     0.0749
   sigma(beta), + free radius tilt (competitor) 0.0782
   correlation(beta, gamma) after marginalising +0.2876

   Run R fitted beta = +0.17188 with a systematic floor of beta_spurious ~ 0.096.
   statistical detection of beta = 0.17188:    2.3 sigma with the class step free,   2.2 sigma with the competitor free
   the experiment is SYSTEMATICS-limited: sigma_stat 0.078 vs sigma_syst 0.096

